# What must never reach the build context.
#
# There was no such file until 2026-09-22, which meant `docker compose build`
# sent the entire working tree to the daemon and `COPY . .` wrote all of it into
# a layer. Three separate problems, in descending order of seriousness.
#
# 1. **`.env` was going into the image.** It is gitignored, so it never reaches
#    the repository — but gitignore says nothing to Docker, and an image is a
#    more distributable artefact than a working tree. Real credentials were
#    being baked into a layer that anyone who can pull the image can read with
#    `docker history`. That is the reason this file exists.
#
# 2. **`data/test_split/` was going into the image.** Section 19 seals it: never
#    trained on, never tuned against, never used to pick a threshold. Shipping
#    it inside the artefact under test is not a breach of the seal by itself,
#    but it puts the answer key in the same box as the exam.
#
# 3. The build was enormously slow. The tree carries seven directories of
#    photographs, a `.venv`, a `.git` and a `web/node_modules`, none of which
#    the wheel needs. `du` on the working tree does not finish in three minutes.
#
# `docker-compose.yml` bind-mounts `./:/app` over the api and worker containers,
# so everything excluded here is still present at runtime for local development.
# What the image itself needs is the nine packages named in `[tool.setuptools]`
# plus `pyproject.toml` and `README.md`, and every one of those is kept.
#
# Deny by name rather than allow by name: an allowlist that misses one package
# fails the `pip install --no-deps .` at the end of the Dockerfile, and it fails
# it confusingly.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- version control and tooling ---------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.playwright-mcp

# --- Python build and runtime artefacts --------------------------------------
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
htmlcov
.coverage

# --- the web app ---------------------------------------------------------
# The api image does not build or serve the frontend; `docker-compose.yml` has a
# separate `web` service for that.
web/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
web/playwright-report
web/test-results

# --- the sealed evaluation set (section 19) ----------------------------------
data/test_split
40_ruler_images

# --- corpora and annotation exports ------------------------------------------
# Photographs, not code. The pipeline reads whatever is mounted or uploaded.
38_images_asked withproperlabelling
all_images
dataset034
dataset034_withoutlabelboxes
new images (1)
new original images
data/annotations
data/declaration_blocks
data/corpus
project-*.json

# --- training ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 14's toolchain is CUDA- and torch-specific and is deliberately not
# installed in this image; its checkpoints and COCO exports are large.
training
bench/*.json

# --- documentation and local scratch -----------------------------------------
docs
rules_and_acts_docs
*.log
*.tmp
